            <ArticleTitle>The &quot;three-in-one block&quot; for treatment of pain in a patient with acute herpes zoster infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>575-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Herpes zoster infection in elderly patients frequently results in disabling pain, carries a high risk of postherpetic neuralgia (PHN), and can pose a significant therapeutic challenge.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We describe a successful use of the perivascular technique of lumbar plexus blockade (&quot;three-in-one block&quot;) for treatment of pain during acute herpes zoster infection in an 82-year-old severely ill patient in whom other modalities were contraindicated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Three-in-one block using 40 mL of 0.25% bupivacaine with 1:300,000 epinephrine resulted in excellent pain relief that lasted for 2 weeks.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The perivascular technique of lumbar plexus blockade may be a useful alternative to epidural and paravertebral techniques of lumbar blockade in the occasional patient for whom these other approaches are contraindicated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
